# expect: a three-clause `for` is `for init; cond; post:` -- two ';' separating three clauses
# Both compilers name this rule since the `s2 < 0` arm was added to
# compiler/parse/parse.ty@_forstmt_into; tychoc1 used to fall through to the
# generic `expected ';', found op ':'`. src/tychoc.c:4102.
fn main():
    for i := 0; i < 3:
        println("x")
